    </link>
    <!--
      All four WHEEL joints carry damping 0 / friction 0. The URDF originally had
      0.2 and 0.1, and those two numbers were what actually capped the vehicle's
      speed, NOT the max_velocity tag.

      Measured, by comparing true world pose against the plugin's wheel odometry:
      with 0.2/0.1 the robot topped out at ~0.5 m/s of real ground speed no matter
      what was commanded (0.5, 1, 2 and 3 m/s all produced 0.43-0.53 m/s), while
      the odometry cheerfully reported the commanded figure because it is dead
      reckoning off the joint encoders and cannot see slip. With 0/0, a 5 m/s
      command produces 4.18 m/s measured, the balance being the acceleration ramp.

      The STEERING joints keep their 0.1/0.01; damping is wanted there, and they
      do not oppose forward motion.
    -->
    <joint name='front_left_wheel_joint' type='revolute'>
      <pose relative_to='front_left_steering_knuckle'>0 0 0 -1.5708 0 0</pose>
      <parent>front_left_steering_knuckle</parent>
      <child>front_left_wheel</child>
      <axis>
        <xyz>0 0 1</xyz>
        <limit>
          <lower>-10000000000000000</lower>
          <upper>10000000000000000</upper>
        </limit>
        <dynamics>
          <damping>0.0</damping>
          <friction>0.0</friction>
          <spring_reference>0</spring_reference>
          <spring_stiffness>0</spring_stiffness>
        </dynamics>
      </axis>
    </joint>
    <link name='front_left_wheel'>
      <pose relative_to='front_left_wheel_joint'>0 0 0 0 0 0</pose>
      <inertial>
        <pose>0 0 0 0 0 0</pose>
        <mass>0.5</mass>
        <inertia>
          <ixx>0.000531</ixx>
